# Jarvis (stage 1-2 prototype)

Push-to-talk assistant: speech in, command routing, voice out.
Commands: "open <app>", "call <contact>", "weather", "what time is it", "check mail".
No third-party libraries; no API keys.

## Get an installable APK without Android Studio
1. Create a new empty GitHub repository and upload everything in this folder (keep the .github folder).
2. Open the repo's Actions tab, run "Build APK" (it also runs on every push).
3. When it finishes, download the artifact "jarvis-debug-apk", unzip, and copy app-debug.apk to your phone.
4. Open it on the phone and allow "Install unknown apps" for your file manager or browser.

## Or build locally
Open this folder in Android Studio, let it sync, then Run on a USB-connected phone (USB debugging on).

## Test checklist
- Tap mic, say "what time is it" -> spoken time
- "open Gmail" / "open Chrome" -> app opens
- "call <name in your contacts>" -> dialer opens with the number (set autoCall = true in MainActivity.kt to dial directly)
- "weather" -> needs location permission, internet, and a recent location fix (open Google Maps once first)
- Type the same commands in the text box to separate recognition problems from logic problems

